d flexibility while considering safety. T6 appears least connected to your hand and opponents' exposures. Your hand has W tiles and honors; T6 is isolated. Discarding T6 maintains your W9 pair and potential for W8/W6 connections. Also, opponents have not shown much interest in T6. F1 could be kept for wind points, but with only one left, the chance to pung is very low; however, keeping it might allow a pair if you draw another, which is possible. But your hand already has potential pairs (W9). Given you need two more melds, discarding an isolated tile like T6 is reasonable.\n\nFinal choice: Play T6 to reduce suit clutter and keep options open with W tiles and honors.\n\nAnswer: Play T6"}
